   "unmapped": [
    "Feedback is a single user choice from the offered assortment plus outside option, drawn from an MNL choice model with utilities f_w*(x_ti); reward is the expected revenue sum_i p(i|S) r_ti",
    "Utility f_w is a non-linear parametric function (e.g. neural network) of the context with parameter w in R^{d_w}; bounded value, gradient and Hessian in w (C_f, C_g, C_h)",
    "Contexts must be i.i.d. from an unknown distribution during Phase I (first t_0 rounds); afterwards may be adversarial",
    "Generalized geometric condition (growth / local strong convexity mu) on the expected squared loss around the equivalence set W*",
    "The learner knows C_h, kappa and mu (used in tuning lambda, beta_t, t_0 and the optimistic utility)",
    "Paper's N (number of items) maps to K; paper's K (max assortment size) maps to m"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "at each round $t$, the agent observes a set of feature vectors for all items, denoted by $X_t := \\{ \\xb_{t1}, \\ldots, \\xb_{tN} \\} \\subset \\mathbb{R}^d$ ... the agent selects an assortment $S_t = \\{i_1, \\dots, i_l\\} \\in \\mathcal{S}:= \\{ S \\subset [N]: |S| \\le K \\}$ ... and observes a user choice $i_t \\in S_t \\cup \\{0\\}$ ... modeled by the MNL choice model"
  }
