    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Suppose Assumptions 1,2,3 and 4 hold. For any $\\delta \\in (0,1)$, if we set ... $t_0 = \\lceil \\kappa^{-3/2} d_w \\sqrt{T} \\rceil$, $\\lambda = \\tilde{\\Ocal}(\\kappa^{-5/2} \\mu^{-1} d_w \\sqrt{T})$, $\\beta_t = \\tilde{\\Ocal} ( \\mu^{-2} \\kappa^{-4} d_w )$ ... then with probability at least $1 - 2\\delta$, Algorithm 1 achieves ... $\\mathrm{Regret}_{T} = \\tilde{ \\Ocal } ( \\kappa^{-3/2} d_w \\sqrt{T} + \\kappa^{-2} \\mu^{-1} d_w \\sqrt{T} )$."
   },
